# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored — never commit real keys.
# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web app.
#
# Neither of these carries a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so Next.js keeps them on the
# server. Nothing in the browser needs them: every Supabase call happens in a
# Server Component, a Server Action, or proxy.ts. The publishable key would be
# safe to expose — RLS is the real protection — but there is no reason to.
#
# Add a client-side Supabase call later (realtime, an auth listener) and the
# prefix has to come back, on both variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scraper only (scraper/.env locally, GitHub Actions secrets in CI).
# service_role bypasses RLS entirely — never let this near the web app.
# SUPABASE_URL above is reused as-is.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Gmail SMTP — an App Password, not your account password.
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (needs 2FA enabled)
# GMAIL_ADDRESS=
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
